{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["Esau took his wives from the daughters of Canaan — the careful reader will note that in the first section of the generations of Yitzhak it says: Yehudit daughter of Be'eri the Hittite, Basmat daughter of Elon the Hittite, Machalat daughter of Yishma'el. And in this section the daughter of Be'eri is not mentioned at all, neither her name nor her father's name, but Elon and Yishma'el, the fathers of his first two wives, are mentioned — the daughters' names having been swapped, as we find in several places: Basmat daughter of Elon is here called Adah daughter of Elon, and Machalat daughter of Yishma'el is here called Basmat. Therefore one must say that Yehudit daughter of Be'eri died without sons, but the daughter of Elon and the daughter of Yishma'el had sons, who are specified here. And Oholivamah daughter of Anah daughter of Tziv'on the Hivite he took afterward, after he went to settle in Mount Se'ir and intermarried with the people of Se'ir the Hivite, as written before us — for Oholivamah was the daughter of Anah daughter of Tziv'on son of Se'ir the Horite, and also Timna, concubine of Elifaz, is listed there among the people of Se'ir. And since Oholivamah was his last wife, therefore he mentions her and her sons last in all these sections."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:20.782439329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}